title: National Bolshevism in Hamburg
subtitle: Laufenberg and Wolffheim preach a people's war against Versailles.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 8 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 1

= National Bolshevism in Hamburg

Heinrich Laufenberg, once chairman of the Hamburg workers' and soldiers' council, and Fritz Wolffheim have gone further than anyone in the party. The German bourgeoisie, they say, has sold the nation to the Entente. The working class must lead a revolutionary people's war against Versailles beside Soviet Russia, and any officer who will fight is welcome.

They also want no Zentrale, no union work and no elections, and the Hamburg district follows them. [? if versailles_line = 2 : In May the Zentrale let their line on Versailles stand. They took that as a licence. ?] The autumn congress is coming, and every word from Hamburg is ammunition for one side or the other.

- @condemn: Condemn the Hamburg line in a circular.
- @tolerate: Say nothing, for the sake of unity.
- @dockers: Send organisers to win Hamburg's dockers away from their leaders.

@condemn
subtitle: Bremen dislikes Laufenberg's nationalism, and may break with Hamburg. Hamburg will call it a declaration of war.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_natbol = 1;
Q.natbol_line = 1;
Q.district_hamburg_loyalty -= 8;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.ecci('lenin', 4);
!}

@tolerate
subtitle: A young party cannot afford heresy trials. Lenin will not understand.
on-arrival: {!
Q.natbol_line = 2;
Q.unity += 3;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 1;
RG.ecci('lenin', -6);
!}

The nationalist officers' clubs of Hamburg send observers to our meetings.

@dockers
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Slow, and it may split Hamburg before the congress does.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.heid_natbol = 1;
Q.natbol_line = 3;
Q.district_hamburg_loyalty += 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Young organisers go to Blohm and Voss with a simple message: we are against Versailles and against the generals, both. An opposition to Laufenberg begins to form on the docks.
